Chapter: PlugDeepRec
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 NON-TAIL RECURSION, ONE FRAME PER ELEMENT. `sum-to` recurses and then adds, so
 no tail-call rewriting can flatten it; this is the shape every list walk in the
 safari port has. The question is how much wasm stack one frame costs, because
 the answer decides whether a module the plug emits can run in a BROWSER, where
 the stack is about 1 MB and there is no flag to raise it.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  sum-to : Integer -> Integer
  sum-to (n) = if n <= 0 then 0 else n + sum-to (n - 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("sum-to 1000   = " & show (sum-to 1000))
    print-line-uni ("sum-to 10000  = " & show (sum-to 10000))
    print-line-uni ("sum-to 50000  = " & show (sum-to 50000))
  end
